  "merge_note": "Regional events built by grouping country-level EMDAT events on (year, type, subtype). Where web research (Wikipedia cyclone season articles, JTWC, BoM, FMS reports) clearly identifies distinct events within a group — e.g. a North Pacific typhoon vs a South Pacific cyclone in the same year, or two named cyclones affecting different country sets — the group is split into separate events. The 'name' field gives the identified storm name; the 'note' field explains the split rationale or lists constituent storms when decomposition is impossible. Affected, deaths, damage_usd, and events_count are summed across the countries in each sub-event. When a single country was hit by multiple events of the same type/subtype in the same year, EMDAT has already aggregated them and the data cannot be decomposed — those groups retain a note listing the known constituent storms.",
